    "pdpPlainTextPreview": "WE ARE STRENGTHENING ACCOUNT SECURITY AND PROTECTING YOUR ACCESS WITH 2 STEP VERIFICATION. FIND OUT MORE Home Great Engravers The William IV Crown The Merlen Shield Silver Two-Coin Set Share via NEW Silver Proof The Merlen Shield Silver Two-Coin Set Limited Edition 100 Price: £550.00 Read Reviews EMAIL ME WHEN IN STOCK Email Me When In Stock PRODUCT CODE: HISGEMSS The set includes the 2026 UK commemorative coin celebrating Merlen’s exquisite heraldic shield design The commemorative edition is struck in 2oz of 999 fine silver and finished to Proof standard Includes an original 1834 half-crown that features William Wyon’s acclaimed bare-headed portrait of William IV on the obverse Silver Proof Read the full description YOU MIGHT ALSO BE INTERESTED IN ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Coin £62.46 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2022 1 oz Silver Bullion Coin £61.26 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 5 Genius Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Queen Elizabeth II 2026 UK £5 Brilliant Uncirculated Coin £17.50 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 4 Mastermind Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Gold Bullion Coin £3,495.05 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Twenty-Five Coin Tube £1,481.50 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 3 Decoder Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 2 Explorer Medal and Collector Folder £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET 75 Years of Dennis the Menace 2026 UK 50p Brilliant Uncirculated Coin £15.00 In Stock Jean Baptiste Merlen was a talented engraver who contributed significantly to nineteenth-century British numismatics. Known for his refined approach to heraldry, he created some of the most enduring shield designs to appear on coins produced by The Royal Mint. This two-coin silver set brings together the 2026 commemorative coin honouring his reverse for the 1831 William IV crown with an original half-crown. Dated 1834, the half-crown reflects the same stylistic precision and heraldic sensibilities that shaped Merlen’s work. Presented side by side, the coins offer collectors a clear view of the engraver’s symbolism and neoclassical refinement. SPECIFICATION William IV Crown 2026 UK 2oz Silver Proof Coin Specification Value Denomination £5 Alloy 999 Fine Silver Weight 62.86 g Diameter 40.00mm Reverse Designer Jean Baptiste Merlen Specification Value Obverse Designer Martin Jennings Quality Proof Year 2026 Pure Metal Type Silver Edge Milled 1834 Halfcrown Specification Value Denomination Half Crown Alloy .925 Sterling Silver Weight 14.140g Diameter 32.31mm Reverse Designer Jean Baptiste Merlen Specification Value Obverse Designer William Wyon Quality Circulating Year 1834 Condition Fine or better CUSTOMER REVIEWS"
